    seed_jit_coverage_self_hosted_compiler_2026-08-21, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-61127: the doc's original premise (per-function FallbackReason census) was already refuted in its own body (on the lint lane every de-JIT is whole-module); the row's redirected acceptance gate scripts/check/check-lint-runs-on-jit.shs was RED (2026-11-11..13 addenda, blocker named Future.map ANY-ANY closure boundary). On the fresh seed the blocker had MOVED: gate failed with unresolved external symbol check_short_grammar_refactor (cross-module Simple function; per-module JIT does not link imported Simple functions) - the recorded Future.map refusal no longer fires (async rework monomorphizes i64 thunks); census still emits exactly one whole-module decision line (premise re-confirmed dead). Mechanism: after the 0ccbe593404 easy_fix refactor the lint CLI callers imported the wrapper via the package re-export chain (compiler.tools.fix.rules) whose body never reaches the JIT unit; the module-file import (rules.impl_.lint_short_grammar) flattens and does. Fix: src/app/io/cli_lint_commands.spl:25 and src/app/io/_CliCommands/run_commands.spl:14 repoint the import at the owning module file (1 line each; use lazy unchanged); check-lint-runs-on-jit.shs verdict grep now accepts Lint completed with 0 error in addition to Lint passed (the old grep was stale since the honest-receipt lint rework; zero-error-only, exit-code and de-JIT checks unchanged). Verification: gate PASS - 1 invocation, JIT lane taken, 0 de-JIT in 36.1s vs 343s interpreted, stdout byte-identical (0 errors, 138 warnings); regression spec test/01_unit/compiler/seed_lint_entry_stays_on_jit_lane_spec.spl GREEN 1/1 on the fix, RED verified with pre-fix imports (receipt engine=interpreter demoted=yes); no new warnings (lint diagnostics on the edited files byte-identical before/after). NEW EXPOSED BLOCKER recorded per the cap rule as lint_forced_jit_clean_target_unwrap_none_2026-11-27: with the closure truly on JIT, linting a warning-free target on the forced lane crashes unwrap on None rc 127 (~18s, any clean file) - masked pre-fix because every forced-JIT lint de-JITted first; suspect linter.last_resolved_config.unwrap() in 90.tools/lint/_LintMain/entry_and_fixes.spl; default lane interpreter-by-design so no default user affected. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/seed_lint_entry_stays_on_jit_lane_spec.spl prevention=scripts/check/check-lint-runs-on-jit.shs"

